WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.180
Because most reality TV shows are about as
authentic as a three dollar bill, lots of

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.920
these series will often bring in experts on
various subjects to boost their credibility.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.230
History Channel's Pawn Stars often makes use
of specialists who themselves have become

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.880
quite famous thanks to frequent appearances.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.180
These men and women can help determine whether
a big ticket item is the real deal or just

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.500
a piece of junk.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.380
But who are they really?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.750
Here's a look at what you don't know about
the 'experts' on Pawn Stars.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.750
Bob Yuhas

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:35.660
An antiques restorer who first appeared on
Pawn Stars during Season 8, Bob Yuhas specializes

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.640
in "restoring, repairing and the conservation
of antiques."

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.410
In his own words, he can make "old things
look new and new things look old."

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:48.720
Yuhas' restoration abilities are no joke,
although his line delivery could use a little

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.720
work —

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.670
“This safe was built 140 years ago with
old world craftsmanship.”

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:58.649
— which is odd, because in addition to Yuhas'
work with antiques, he's also an actor.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:04.170
If you're a fan of the Food Network reality
series Mystery Diners, he might look familiar.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.250
He appeared in an episode titled "Night Shift"
as the buddy of a late-night bartender that

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.350
was supposedly undermining his unsuspecting
boss.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.610
We say "supposedly" because as Radar Online
reveals, the show was busted for fakery.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.650
With Pawn Stars dodging its own accusations
of staging, Bob Yuhas' addition to the series'

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.830
list of experts feels somewhat ironic.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.960
Bill Tsagrinos

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.299
Specializing in collecting and restoring classic
vehicles, Bill Tsagrinos runs The Underground

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:36.950
Garage, where he fixes up awesome rides like
his signature 1967 Volkswagen Bus.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.659
Before Tsagrinos appeared on Pawn Stars, his
love of cars played out on the Bill Goldberg-hosted

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:46.320
reality TV show known as Bullrun, where he
and his brother George successfully auditioned

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.909
to appear during the second season.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:52.950
The brothers raced their 1967 Volkswagen bus
against 11 other teams.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.740
Sadly, they didn't win.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:59.729
While Pawn Stars fans know Tsagrinos primarily
for his love and knowledge about old cars,

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:02.920
there's another industry for which he's known:
tiles.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:08.539
Tsagrinos founded T Brothers Tile, a company
"specializing in tile, granite, laminate,

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:12.730
wood, carpet, window coverings, and water
jet cutting services."

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:17.099
The company claims they've installed more
than 26 million square feet of tile — enough

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:20.180
to cover just over 450 football fields.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.109
Dr. Phineas T. Kastle

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:27.431
One can't help but instantly become a fan
of the charmingly eccentric Dr. Phineas T.

00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:30.250
Kastle, better known as "Doc Phineas."

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.659
When the guys at Pawn Stars have no idea whether
an item is authentic or even what the heck

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:38.279
it is, Phineas is the expert they bring in
to figure it out.

00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:43.739
In addition to his vast knowledge of antiques,
Doc Phineas is a huge steampunk fan, so much

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:48.529
so that he helped produce the Las Vegas-based
Steamathon, a weekend-long celebration of

00:02:48.529 --> 00:02:50.019
all things steampunk.

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:54.450
Although known as "Doc" Phineas, he could
technically change his name to professor.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.349
According to Phineas, he's taught college
classes for over 45 years.

00:02:57.349 --> 00:03:03.620
Docs Phineas is also an actor, singer, and
he's known to dance every now and then too.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.159
Rock, on, doc!

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:06.449
Sean Rich

00:03:06.449 --> 00:03:11.709
The owner of Tortuga Trading, Sean Rich is
an "antique arms and armor specialist" as

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:14.489
well as an expert on shipwreck treasure.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:18.499
This may be why Disney turned to Rich when
filming Pirates of the Caribbean.

00:03:18.499 --> 00:03:22.319
He was generous enough to lease and sell items
for the making of the second and third movie,

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:27.359
and he also provided props for AMC's American
Revolution-based drama Turn.

00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:32.040
Rich appeared on Pawn Stars series in 2011,
but then walked away because, according to

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.629
Rich, both the Pawn Stars producers and the
History Channel required an "exclusive contract."

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:43.159
Rich said, "[The contract would] lock me down,
control me, my business, future, my appearance,

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:45.159
how I make a living to provide for my family."

00:03:45.159 --> 00:03:49.920
In 2013, Rich opted to hop over to National
Geographic to host and star in the series

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.019
Lords of War.

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:54.919
The History Channel must have come around
eventually, because he returned to Pawn Stars

00:03:54.919 --> 00:03:56.849
in 2014.

00:03:56.849 --> 00:03:58.650
Jesse Amoroso

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.269
Pawn Stars' vintage musical instrument and
amplifier specialist, Jesse Amoroso happens

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:05.609
to own the famous Cowtown Guitars.

00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:10.919
Amoroso and his wife Roxie, who also appears
at Cowtown, were known locally for their "sleaze-rock

00:04:10.919 --> 00:04:14.639
band" Pigasus before buying Cowtown in 2011.

00:04:14.639 --> 00:04:20.130
Fun fact: Cowtown was actually founded in
1990 by Bob Seger touring guitarist Mark Chatfield.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.520
Cowtown has thrived under the ownership of
Amoroso, thanks in part to the celebrity he's

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.650
gained as a frequently featured expert on
Pawn Stars.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:32.560
The boom in business might be why Amoroso
ultimately decided to relocate — he's now

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.010
"within walking distance of the legendary
Gold &amp; Silver Pawn."

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:40.970
Through Cowtown, Amoroso happens to own "one
of the largest collections of vintage instruments

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.100
in North America."

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.030
For a true music lover, it doesn't get much
better than that.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.370
Jeremy Brown

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:51.510
It seems pretty common for Pawn Stars experts
to relocate their businesses to be closer

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.910
to the Gold &amp; Silver Pawn.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:58.360
Jeremy Brown, the show's go-to sports memorabilia
guy, moved his Ultimate Sport Cards &amp; Memorabilia

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.090
business in 2012.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.620
Brown's business was doing pretty well for
itself before he made the big move, but he's

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.980
said he wanted to "fully embrace the opportunity
that the show has provided and be near other

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.370
fellow experts."

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.430
Brown said that his life as a sports memorabilia
expert began with an addiction to collecting

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.060
baseball cards.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:19.300
According to Sports Collectors Daily, Brown
feels working with Pawn Stars is "an absolute

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.910
blessing" as the show allows him to share
his love of sports memorabilia "with millions

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.370
of people."

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:26.370
Steve Grad

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:31.800
A Professional Sports Authenticator who appeared
on Pawn Stars between 2013 and 2014, Steve

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:36.020
Grad got caught up in some embarrassing controversies
that make it very unlikely he'll reappear

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.800
on the show anytime soon.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.920
The trouble started when Grad found himself
at the center of a 2011 lawsuit.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:46.550
Apparently, his company has tried to pass
off a signature as belonging to famed aviator

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.830
Charles Lindbergh.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.860
Lindbergh's own daughter came forward with
an expert and successfully challenged the

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:52.860
claim.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.980
It turned out that Grad's "expert opinion"
had cost collectors hundreds of thousands

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.280
of dollars after he allegedly approved scores
of forgeries as legitimate.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:04.740
And it gets worse: despite heavily implying
that he'd been educated at the prestigious

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:09.430
Columbia School of Journalism, further research
determined that Grad had actually attended

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.780
Columbia College Chicago instead, and he never
even graduated.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:18.670
In fact, during a court-ordered deposition,
he’d revealed he'd received no formal training

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:21.500
of any kind to back up his "expert" label.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.520
He instead credits much of what he knows to
being mentored by the "King of Memorabilia"

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:31.330
Bill Mastro — a man who landed in prison
after being busted for various acts of fraud.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.960
Mark Hall-Patton

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:38.120
Unlike fraud Steve Grad, Mark Hall-Patton
was recognized by the Los Angeles Times as

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.730
"the real deal."

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:43.740
Hall-Patton is the museum administrator for
the Clark County Museum system.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.810
Although nicknamed "The Beard of Knowledge,"
he readily admits that if he doesn't know

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.720
something, he's always ready to perform detailed
research.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.880
Most of us would turn to Google, but Hall-Patton
can also pull facts from his personal library

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.700
of over 20,000 books.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:01.310
He's appeared on close to 100 episodes of
Pawn Stars, making him one of the show's better-known

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.310
experts.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.180
His wife, Dr. Colleen Hall-Patton, wrote a
Celebrity Studies article on her husband's

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:11.100
sudden fame, and he even has a group of fanboys
in the Washington State Penitentiary.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.830
And sometimes, for fun, he pretends to be
zombie.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:15.610
No, really.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.200
“Ha, I can’t keep it up.”

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.900
Stuart Lutz

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.350
Appearing on Pawn Stars during its eighth
season, Stuart Lutz authenticates "historic

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:36.700
documents, manuscripts and letters," and he's
also one of the few experts to be granted

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:42.760
a seal of approval by the Appraisers Association
of America "in the field on Books and Manuscripts:

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:43.760
Historic Documents."

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:49.900
Lutz has an online catalog of historic documents,
autographs, letters, and manuscripts, and

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:54.430
also owns one of just three authentic castings
of President Eisenhower's hands, something

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:57.150
that's either really awesome or really creepy.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.550
We can't quite decide.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:03.590
Lutz wrote The Last Leaf, a book about the
last known survivors to witness major historical

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:06.570
events or interact with now deceased celebrities.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.650
That’s…kind of morbid.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.850
Brett Maly

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:15.200
A fine art appraiser who appeared on Pawn
Stars between 2010 and 2014, Brett Maly also

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:20.190
earned a bit of celebrity for his 2011 appraisal
of an authentic Andy Warhol sketch, which

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:23.120
was purchased for just $5 at a garage sale.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.620
Not content to leave the fine art world to
the rich, Maly published a 2014 book called

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:32.759
The Pocket Picker: For Fine Art, which features
a foreword penned by Pawn Stars' Rick Harrison.

00:08:32.759 --> 00:08:36.839
The book is meant to help the average person
procure and profit from fine art…and avoid

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:40.870
selling off rare art that they happen to own
for a meager $5.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:47.120
Interestingly, long before his current highbrow
occupation, Maly worked as a DJ for KOOL 105.5

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:52.309
in Florida, where he was often responsible
for radio voiceovers and board operations.

00:08:52.309 --> 00:08:55.110
So…that's pretty random!

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.749
Rebecca Romney

00:08:56.749 --> 00:09:01.749
The only female expert featured on Pawn Stars,
bibliophile Rebecca Romney's expertise is

00:09:01.749 --> 00:09:04.490
"rare and antiquarian books and documents.

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:08.579
But there's a bit more to her than dusty old
texts: in addition to English, she speaks

00:09:08.579 --> 00:09:13.800
French and Japanese fluently, and can actually
read six languages, including Latin, Ancient

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:14.800
Greek, and Old English.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.860
And, in case you're not impressed by that,
Old English actually looks and sounds like

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:20.620
this:

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:30.389
She also hosted a Reddit "ask me anything"
in 2014, during which she admitted to going

00:09:30.389 --> 00:09:32.899
on double dates with Pawn Stars' Rick Harrison.

00:09:32.899 --> 00:09:37.120
And she once brought filming on the Pawn Stars
set to a halt because a rare book wasn't being

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.790
handled properly.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.959
Now that's a bibliophile.

00:09:40.959 --> 00:09:42.430
Murray Sawchuck

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:46.899
Better known as "Magic Murray," Murray Sawchuck
is easily distinguishable from the other experts

00:09:46.899 --> 00:09:49.589
thanks to his spiky, bleach-blond hairstyle.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:53.480
The celebrity magician and funnyman is called
upon from time to time to give his expert

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.230
opinion on all sorts of "magical items."

00:09:56.230 --> 00:10:00.740
The self-proclaimed "Dennis the Menace of
Magic" is no stranger to the reality TV show

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:01.740
circuit.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.470
He also made appearances on both America's
Got Talent and the reality dating series Blind

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:09.620
Date, which detailed his magical search for
love.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.620
“Hello.”

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:11.260
“Hey, how you doing?”

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:11.880
“How are you?”

00:10:16.209 --> 00:10:20.709
Although things didn't work out with Georgia,
Magic Murray did find eventually love with

00:10:20.709 --> 00:10:25.509
Britain's Got Talent performer Chloe Crawford,
and the couple were married in 2012.

00:10:25.509 --> 00:10:30.790
Sadly, a few years later, Crawford dumped
him for rival illusionist Criss Angel.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:31.790
Harsh.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.230
Well, they say what goes around comes around,
and Crawford was reportedly dumped by Angel

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.529
less than a year after she left Sawchuck.

00:10:38.529 --> 00:10:43.199
Looks like these magicians know how to make
a relationship disappear.

00:10:43.199 --> 00:10:45.050
Matthew C. Shortal

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:49.939
He claims to be an expert on all things military
and aviation — and Matthew C. Shortal definitely

00:10:49.939 --> 00:10:51.860
has the résumé to back it up.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.910
Not only did he achieve the rank of Lieutenant
Colonel in the United States Marines, Shortal

00:10:55.910 --> 00:11:00.940
is also a former U.S. Navy Blue Angel Pilot
and an honest-to-goodness graduate of the

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:02.959
elite TOPGUN program.

00:11:02.959 --> 00:11:08.850
Additionally, Shortal is an avid triathlon
competitor, and has competed in Ironman 70.3

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.149
as part of a team.

00:11:10.149 --> 00:11:13.470
Sounds like he feels the need…for speed.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:19.230
“I feel the need...the need for speed!

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:20.510
Ow!”

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.510
Thanks for watching!

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.970
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.199
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

